WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.070
- I definitely find
specifically with "Boyfriend"

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:03.330
because it was such a huge part

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:06.930
of me finding my own identity
and embracing my queerness.

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:08.970
And it like, makes me emotional
every time I talk about it.

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:13.970
But it was such a like
a key to a gate for me.

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:15.132
- Yeah.

00:00:15.132 --> 00:00:16.410
- And to stepping into
myself wholly in a way

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:19.260
that I never knew if I was
gonna be privileged enough

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:21.360
to find those pieces of myself

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:24.120
and exist as that person, right.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:24.953
'Cause that's like the fear.

00:00:24.953 --> 00:00:26.580
The fear is that you
exist as yourself wholly

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:28.470
and the world cracks
open and everything ends,

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:29.887
and all the lights go out.

00:00:29.887 --> 00:00:31.950
And when the song came out

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:35.040
and when I saw that people were
emotionally connecting to it

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.990
I think I was really
panicked for some reason.

00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:38.190
Just 'cause I wasn't expecting it.

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:39.265
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:39.265 --> 00:00:40.950
- And then over time it was like,

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:44.790
it melded into this gorgeous,
like, something meaningful

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:46.950
for me being something
meaningful for others.

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:48.240
I'm sure you've had that before.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:49.073
- Yeah.

00:00:49.073 --> 00:00:50.100
- It becomes this like,

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:53.160
especially when it's something
about, you know, identity

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.050
and queerness and how
people view themselves.

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:56.010
- Something so personal and intimate.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:58.050
- And finding empowerment in it

00:00:58.050 --> 00:00:59.730
when it's something that can sometimes

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:01.963
feel very heavy to carry alone, identity.

00:01:01.963 --> 00:01:02.796
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:04.560
- And I've found it incredibly special

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.900
and meaningful and such a surprise.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.040
Such a beautiful surprise.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:09.240
- Well we have a surprise for you.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:10.080
- You have a surprise for me?

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:10.913
- Yes, we do.

00:01:10.913 --> 00:01:11.746
- What does that mean?

00:01:11.746 --> 00:01:14.670
- In honor of over one
million records sold, ma'am,

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:17.220
we're excited to present
you with the RIAA Platinum

00:01:18.529 --> 00:01:21.202
(audience drowning Kelly out)

00:01:21.202 --> 00:01:22.194
- Oh my God.

00:01:22.194 --> 00:01:23.657
(Kelly making laser sounds)

00:01:23.657 --> 00:01:24.600
Thank you so much.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.593
- I was so excited when we
found out you were getting it.

00:01:26.593 --> 00:01:28.050
I was like I wanna give it to her.

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:30.870
Dove's latest single is called "Bad Idea"

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:32.820
and it's available wherever
you get your music.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:34.667
Check it out, y'all.

